## Monitoring

- Health endpoint: `GET /api/health` → `{ status: "ok", version, timestamp }` (frontends expose the same shape on `/api/health` or a static path configured in the platform)
- Error tracking: Sentry (SENTRY_DSN in environment)
- Log aggregation: Axiom (AXIOM_TOKEN, AXIOM_DATASET)
- Uptime/alerting: Better Stack (BETTER_STACK_URL or heartbeat URL)
- Alerts: Slack webhook (SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL) or Telegram

## Deployment

Default Lixali target is Cloudflare:

- **Frontend:** Cloudflare Pages — `npm run deploy` via Wrangler
- **Backend:** Cloudflare Workers — `npm run deploy` via Wrangler
- **Production:** `main` branch pushes trigger automatic deployment after checks pass
- **Preview:** branches and pull requests get preview URLs via Cloudflare Pages/Workers

Alternative targets (use the matching skill):

- **AWS:** `deploy-to-aws` (Elastic Beanstalk, Lambda, or ECS depending on project)
- **Custom VPS:** `deploy-to-vps` using [Shipnode](https://github.com/devalade/shipnode)

Environment variables are set in the platform dashboard (Cloudflare Pages/Workers, AWS, or VPS) — never committed to git.

## Database & Migrations

For Cloudflare D1 + Drizzle backend:

- Schema source of truth: `src/db/schema.ts`
- Migrations: `migrations/` at project root (Wrangler compatibility)
- Generate: `npm run db:generate`
- Apply locally: `npm run db:migrate:local`
- Apply to remote: `npm run db:migrate:prod`
- Seed: `npm run db:seed` (manual script, never auto-seed on dev startup)

For Supabase:

- Migrations: `supabase/migrations/`
- Push: `supabase db push`

## Workflows (Inngest)

- Inngest functions live in `src/inngest/`
- Local dev: `npx inngest-cli@latest dev` (or `npm run inngest:dev`)
- Production: sync functions via `inngest-cli` or the Inngest dashboard after Worker/Pages deployment
- Critical functions must be idempotent and retry-aware

## Commit Conventions

- One commit per meaningful change (one feature, one fix, one refactor)
- Never commit `.env.local` or any file with real credentials
- Always run `npm run typecheck` before committing
- Commit `AGENTS.md` changes alongside the code changes they document
- Keep commits in English for consistency across the team
